      'The massacres of 1914–1920 (remembered as the Sayfo, “the sword”) and recent wars in Iraq and Syria have devastated the community in its homeland, and many members now live in Europe and the Americas. The patriarchate moved from Mardin to Homs and then Damascus (1959). The church worships with the Liturgy of St James in Syriac.',
